{%- doc -%}
  Renders the add-to-cart / choose-options / quick-add action row for a product card.

  @param {product} [closest.product] - The product this block acts on. Must be available in the
    rendering context (e.g. as a child of blocks/_product-card.liquid); renders nothing without it.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Mirrors ../design-system/src/react/ProductCard/ProductCardActions.tsx and the Button it wraps: the
  action row at the foot of a product card. It declares no box padding of its own -- padding is four
  merchant settings defaulting to 0, so composition decides; only margin-block-start: auto stays, to
  pin the row to the card's foot.

  It's a direct child of Horizon's blocks/_product-card.liquid, a sibling of mionas-price, and reads
  closest.product -- rendering nothing without one. Unlike a private block it's visible in the block
  picker, since a merchant places and orders it.

  Not a reskin of blocks/add-to-cart.liquid: that block's can_add_to_cart and add_to_cart_text
  parameters only arrive from its parent block, with no schema path to give it product context here.

  Doesn't render snippets/quick-add.liquid (though the branch logic below mirrors it): that snippet's
  styles make the button a floating pill anchored over the card on hover, which isn't this design's
  static full-row action, and there's no setting to opt out of it. This block reproduces its
  structure and the data-* attributes assets/quick-add.js reads, under its own class names instead.

  The button itself still renders through snippets/add-to-cart-button.liquid, for its
  <add-to-cart-component> wrapper, checkmark-burst markup and fly-to-cart binding -- reproducing that
  here would fork behaviour upstream still maintains. It wears blocks/mionas-button.liquid's classes
  rather than its own, since that stylesheet already spends every --button-* token in the shape
  needed; mionas-button.liquid itself can't be reused directly here because it renders an <a>, not a
  submittable form control. Two rules near the bottom of the stylesheet re-override
  .add-to-cart-button's own pressed-state and height, because that selector is equally specific and
  would otherwise win on bundle order.

  The choose-options branch falls back to a plain link rather than a second quick-add dialog, because
  the dialog is a single global element (layout/theme.liquid) keyed to a page-wide #quick-add-dialog
  id -- a second instance per card would collide with it. settings.quick_add is off in this store
  today, but the fallback still needs to work if a merchant re-enables it.

  The Variant setting offers all seven of mionas-button.liquid's variants. The two inverse variants
  only read correctly on dark grounds, and danger exists for destructive actions -- the schema
  leaves that judgement to the merchant rather than restricting the list.

  Known cosmetic overlap: pressing this button also dims the whole card, because
  snippets/product-card-bridge.liquid's `.product-card:active .product-card__content` rule matches
  ancestors of the pressed element too. Left as-is rather than scoping the card's pressed state
  around this block.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product = closest.product
-%}

{%- if product != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign block_settings = block.settings
    assign selected_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
    assign product_form_id = 'MionasAddToCart-' | append: product.id | append: '-' | append: block.id

    assign uses_selling_plans = false
    if product.requires_selling_plan or product.selling_plan_groups.size > 0
      assign uses_selling_plans = true
    endif

    assign can_add_to_cart = false
    if selected_variant.available
      assign can_add_to_cart = true
    endif

    comment
      Each label falls back to the locale string the native path uses -- 'actions.add' and
      'actions.choose' from quick-add.liquid, 'products.product.sold_out' from buy-buttons.liquid --
      so a block left alone stays translated, and a merchant who types a label gets exactly that.

      `| default:` isn't enough alone: a cleared text setting returns an empty string, not nil, so
      default won't substitute for it. Hence the blank checks.
    endcomment
    assign add_to_cart_text = block_settings.label_add
    if add_to_cart_text == blank
      assign add_to_cart_text = 'actions.add' | t
    endif

    unless can_add_to_cart
      assign add_to_cart_text = block_settings.label_sold_out
      if add_to_cart_text == blank
        assign add_to_cart_text = 'products.product.sold_out' | t
      endif
    endunless

    assign choose_options_text = block_settings.label_choose
    if choose_options_text == blank
      assign choose_options_text = 'actions.choose' | t
    endif

    comment
      Only a single-variant product resolves to one variant at render time, so only it gets a real
      add-to-cart form; everything else -- multiple options, or selling plans regardless of variant
      count -- goes to the choose branch. Mionas cards render no swatches, so quick-add.liquid's
      swatch-resolves-variant case (which can flip choose -> add client-side) doesn't apply here.
    endcomment
    assign render_add = false
    if product.variants_count == 1 and uses_selling_plans == false
      assign render_add = true
    endif

    assign quick_add_modal_available = false
    if settings.quick_add or settings.mobile_quick_add
      assign quick_add_modal_available = true
    endif


    comment
      The class vocabulary comes from snippets/mionas-button-class.liquid, the same snippet
      blocks/mionas-button.liquid renders, rather than being rebuilt here. add-to-cart-button is
      passed as the prefix since it's Horizon's own hook for the checkmark-burst/fly-to-cart
      animation CSS and has to stay on regardless of variant.

      The rules for these classes live in snippets/mionas-button-styles.liquid, rendered globally by
      snippets/design-system-bridge.liquid rather than as a block-level stylesheet tag -- a
      block-level tag only ships on pages where that block renders, and this block doesn't render
      mionas-button.liquid, so the vocabulary would resolve to nothing on a collection page.
    endcomment
    comment
      One line on purpose: inside a liquid tag every line is its own tag, so a render split across
      lines parses as an unknown tag named after its first argument. Theme check does not catch it;
      the dev server's upload does.
    endcomment
    capture button_classes
      render 'mionas-button-class', variant: block_settings.variant, size: block_settings.size, full_width: block_settings.full_width, prefix: 'add-to-cart-button'
    endcapture

    comment
      The icon is hidden via CSS rather than by not rendering it: snippets/add-to-cart-button.liquid
      emits it unconditionally with no toggle parameter, and display: none also removes it from the
      accessibility tree, which is correct since it's decorative and already aria-hidden.

      The modifier class sits on the wrapper, not the button, so one class governs both the cart icon
      (add branch) and the plus icon (choose/fallback branches) under icon_only.

      show_icon and icon_only are mutually exclusive: icon_only hides the show_icon setting in the
      editor, but a previously stored show_icon: false survives that, and both together would render
      neither icon nor label.
    endcomment
    assign wrapper_classes = 'mionas-add-to-cart'
    if block_settings.icon_only
      assign wrapper_classes = wrapper_classes | append: ' mionas-add-to-cart--icon-only'
    elsif block_settings.show_icon == false
      assign wrapper_classes = wrapper_classes | append: ' mionas-add-to-cart--no-icon'
    endif
  -%}

  {% render 'add-to-cart-button-styles' %}
  {% render 'fly-to-cart-styles' %}

  <div
    class="{{ wrapper_classes }} spacing-style"
    style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: block_settings %}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    {%- if render_add -%}
      <product-form-component
        data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
        data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
        on:submit="/handleSubmit"
      >
        {%- comment -%}
          ProductFormComponent.requiredRefs is ['variantId', 'liveRegion'] (product-form.js:206) --
          the component does not initialise without both, so neither the hidden input's ref nor this
          region is optional.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div
          class="visually-hidden"
          aria-live="assertive"
          role="status"
          aria-atomic="true"
          ref="liveRegion"
        ></div>
        {%- form 'product', product, id: product_form_id, novalidate: 'novalidate', data-type: 'add-to-cart-form' -%}
          <input
            type="hidden"
            name="id"
            ref="variantId"
            value="{{ selected_variant.id }}"
            {% if can_add_to_cart == false %}
              disabled
            {% endif %}
          >
          <input
            type="hidden"
            name="quantity"
            value="{% if selected_variant.quantity_rule.min %}{{ selected_variant.quantity_rule.min }}{% else %}1{% endif %}"
          >
          {%- if block_settings.icon_only and can_add_to_cart == false -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              snippets/add-to-cart-button.liquid only emits its icon when can_add_to_cart, so a
              sold-out product gets none -- and the icon-only rule's font-size: 0 then collapses the
              label too, leaving a blank disabled square (verified on /collections/comprar-cookies).
              Bypassing the snippet here is safe because this branch is disabled and can never fire
              the checkmark-burst animation the snippet exists to provide.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              The literal "button" class is what base.css's `.button:disabled` opacity/cursor rule
              hooks onto -- the other path gets it for free from add-to-cart-button.liquid, but this
              branch bypasses that snippet.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <button
              class="button {{ button_classes }}"
              type="submit"
              name="add"
              disabled
            >
              <span class="svg-wrapper" aria-hidden="true">
                {{- 'icon-unavailable.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
              </span>
              {{- add_to_cart_text -}}
            </button>
          {%- else -%}
            {% render 'add-to-cart-button',
              add_to_cart_text: add_to_cart_text,
              class: button_classes,
              can_add_to_cart: can_add_to_cart,
              show_icon: can_add_to_cart,
              product: product
            %}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endform -%}
      </product-form-component>
    {%- elsif quick_add_modal_available -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        QuickAddComponent finds the product URL via this.closest('product-card') and that element's
        refs.productCardLink -- Horizon's own snippets/product-card.liquid supplies both, so this
        button works wherever that card renders it.

        data-quick-add-button is fixed at 'choose' and data-renders-both-buttons is omitted, so
        QuickAddComponent's productSelect handler returns early instead of flipping to a nonexistent
        add button.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <quick-add-component
        class="mionas-add-to-cart__quick-add"
        data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
        data-quick-add-button="choose"
        data-product-options-count="{{ product.options.size }}"
        data-uses-selling-plans="{{ uses_selling_plans }}"
      >
        {%- comment -%}
          type="button" is explicit: submit is the default, and QuickAddComponent opens a dialog
          rather than submitting anything. Same reasoning as quick-add.liquid:127.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The add branch gets its icon free from snippets/add-to-cart-button.liquid. These two
          branches build their own markup, so icon_only has to supply it here or the font-size: 0
          rule below would leave an empty box.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <button
          class="{{ button_classes }}"
          type="button"
          name="add"
          on:click="quick-add-component/handleClick"
        >
          {%- if block_settings.icon_only -%}
            <span class="svg-wrapper" aria-hidden="true">
              {{- 'icon-plus.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {{- choose_options_text -}}
        </button>
      </quick-add-component>
    {%- else -%}
      <a class="{{ button_classes }}" href="{{ product.url }}">
        {%- if block_settings.icon_only -%}
          <span class="svg-wrapper" aria-hidden="true">
            {{- 'icon-plus.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {{- choose_options_text -}}
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /* No padding declared on purpose: padding is four range settings (via spacing-style.liquid)
     defaulting to 0, so this block imposes no inset of its own and the composition decides -- the
     same mechanism blocks/_product-card.liquid exposes for the card itself. Spacing above the button
     still comes from the card's flex `gap`, not this block.

     margin-block-start: auto stays -- it pins the row to the card's foot so buttons line up across a
     grid row regardless of how titles wrap. */
  .mionas-add-to-cart {
    margin-block-start: auto;
  }

  /* Hides the icon when Show icon is off. Targets add-to-cart-button.liquid's own icon span, which
     is aria-hidden, so display: none removes it from the accessibility tree too. */
  .mionas-add-to-cart--no-icon .add-to-cart-icon {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Icon-only mode: font-size: 0 collapses the label, since add-to-cart-button.liquid emits it as a
     bare text node with nothing to target directly -- it stays in the accessibility tree as the
     button's accessible name. The icon survives because .svg-wrapper is sized in rem, not em.

     (0,2,0) specificity is needed to outrank whichever size class is selected; aspect-ratio squares
     the button to the height that size sets, rather than naming a fixed width. */
  .mionas-add-to-cart--icon-only .mionas-button {
    font-size: 0;
    padding-inline: 0;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
  }

  .mionas-add-to-cart__quick-add {
    display: block;
  }

  /* The pressed state is a real collision, not a specificity problem: mionas-button presses with
     `transform: scale()`, while .add-to-cart-button:active presses with separate `scale`/`translate`
     properties, so both apply and the button visibly double-presses. Zeroing Horizon's two
     properties here leaves mionas-button's own transform/opacity as the only pressed state. */
  .mionas-add-to-cart .mionas-button:active {
    scale: 1;
    translate: none;
  }

  /* Second collision, same shape: .add-to-cart-button sets `height: var(--height-buy-buttons)`
     (52px), which ties with and wins over mionas-button's own height. Re-asserted here per size --
     everything else mionas-button declares (padding, font-size, radius, colours) comes through
     untouched. If mionas-button.liquid ever gains a size, add it here too. */
  .mionas-add-to-cart .mionas-button {
    height: var(--button-size-md-height);
  }

  .mionas-add-to-cart .mionas-button--sm {
    height: var(--button-size-sm-height);
  }

  .mionas-add-to-cart .mionas-button--lg {
    height: var(--button-size-lg-height);
  }

  /* mionas-button.liquid only ever renders an <a>, so it styles [aria-disabled="true"] and has no
     :disabled rule. A sold-out product here is a real disabled <button>, which needs the same
     token. */
  .mionas-add-to-cart .mionas-button:disabled {
    opacity: var(--button-state-disabled-opacity);
    cursor: default;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Mionas: Add to cart",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Text"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_add",
      "label": "Add to cart label",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's own wording, which stays translated per language."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_choose",
      "label": "Choose options label",
      "info": "Shown on products with more than one variant, which open the variant picker instead of adding straight away."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_sold_out",
      "label": "Sold out label"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Icon"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "icon_only",
      "label": "Icon only",
      "info": "Hides the label and shows only the icon. The label stays as the button's accessible name, so screen readers still announce it.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_icon",
      "label": "Show cart icon",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Only the add-to-cart button has an icon; the choose-options button never does.",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_only == false }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Style"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "variant",
      "label": "Variant",
      "options": [
        { "value": "primary", "label": "Primary" },
        { "value": "secondary", "label": "Secondary" },
        { "value": "outline", "label": "Outline" },
        { "value": "ghost", "label": "Ghost" },
        { "value": "danger", "label": "Danger" },
        { "value": "inverse-primary", "label": "Inverse primary" },
        { "value": "inverse-ghost", "label": "Inverse ghost" }
      ],
      "default": "primary"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "size",
      "label": "Size",
      "options": [
        { "value": "sm", "label": "Small" },
        { "value": "md", "label": "Medium" },
        { "value": "lg", "label": "Large" }
      ],
      "default": "md"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "full_width",
      "label": "Full width",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "t:settings.top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "t:settings.bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-inline-start",
      "label": "t:settings.left",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-inline-end",
      "label": "t:settings.right",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Mionas: Add to cart",
      "category": "t:categories.product"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
